{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Peoples, the mountain they will call.</b> Because Zebulun dwells on the shore of ships, his wealth will be great, and this is \"for they suck the abundance of the seas,\" and it is from the root of גמלים שפעת (abundance of camels)." "<b>And hidden treasures buried in sand.</b> It has no [parallel] brother, and its meaning is like טמוני (buried), likewise אדמת עפר. The sense is that they will have great wealth, until they bury it in sand, and because of their wealth the majority of them will come to the mountain of HaShem, to slaughter thanksgiving offerings to HaShem."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:32.156162459Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}